flowchart TB
  accTitle: GP-B&#58; Gaussian-space GP + invertible observation flow
  accDescr: GP-B&#58; Gaussian-space GP + invertible observation flow&#59; arrows follow patient context and measurements to predictive distributions and training objectives.
  baseline["Patient baseline s&#58; entry covariates"]
  class baseline input
  past["Recorded causal prefix Events / measurements / updates"]
  class past input
  encoder["Common causal Transformer H₀ = E&#40;prefix&#41;"]
  class encoder history
  query["Query age t + feature ID d Arbitrary, irregular times"]
  class query input
  context["Fixed prefix + query context cₜd = &#91;s, H₀, t, e_d&#93;"]
  class context context
  prior["Multi-output GP prior f ∼ GP&#40;mθ, kθ&#41; Learned mean + PSD cross-feature kernel"]
  class prior latent
  observed["Available measurements D Irregular &#40;t, d, y&#41; records"]
  class observed input
  transform["Forward observation flow g = Tθ&#40;y&#59; c&#41;, with log &#124;J_T&#124; Network predicts invertible flow parameters"]
  class transform flow
  posterior["Exact Gaussian conditioning p&#40;g* &#124; Tθ&#40;D&#41;&#41;, covariance K + Σ g = f + εG in Gaussian space"]
  class posterior latent
  inverse["Inverse observation flow y* = Tθ⁻¹&#40;g*&#59; c*&#41;"]
  class inverse flow
  output["Return clinical units Asymmetric densities / tail shapes Mean / quantiles / joint samples"]
  class output output
  loss["Train&#58; exact change-of-variables NLL −log N&#40;Tθ&#40;y&#41;&#59; m, K + Σ&#41; − log &#124;J_T&#124;"]
  class loss loss
  past --> encoder
  baseline --> context
  encoder --> context
  query --> context
  context --> prior
  observed --> transform
  context -->|Condition flow parameters| transform
  transform -->|Transformed measurements| posterior
  prior -->|Gaussian-space mean / kernel + noise| posterior
  posterior -->|Joint Gaussian-space draws g*| inverse
  context -->|Same invertible flow at query| inverse
  inverse -->|Undo training standardisation| output
  transform -.-> loss
  prior -.-> loss
